/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Samuel chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1samuel", [
{n:6, name:"The Ark Returned", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 6:12",verse:"And the kine took the straight way to the way of Beth-shemesh, and went along the highway, lowing as they went, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left; and the lords of the Philistines went after them unto the border of Beth-shemesh."}, facts:["Did you know the Philistines' own priests quoted the Exodus to their leaders, warning them not to harden their hearts the way Pharaoh did (1 Samuel 6:6)?","Did you know the test of the milch kine was set to prove God's hand: cows never yoked, parted from their calves, yet they walked straight to Beth-shemesh, lowing, without turning aside (1 Samuel 6:7, 12)?","Did you know the great stone of Abel, where the ark was set down in Joshua's field, was still standing when the record was written (1 Samuel 6:18)?"], questions:[
{q:"How long had the ark of the LORD been in the country of the Philistines?", options:["Seven months","Seven years","Forty days","Twelve months"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:1",verse:"And the ark of the LORD was in the country of the Philistines seven months.", insight:"Seven months in enemy hands; God let the ark sit captive to prove that no one can hold Him hostage."},
{q:"Whom did the Philistines call for counsel about the ark?", options:["The priests and the diviners","The five lords","The king of Egypt","Their army captains"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:2",verse:"And the Philistines called for the priests and the diviners, saying, What shall we do to the ark of the LORD? tell us wherewith we shall send it to his place.", insight:"They asked their own wise men what to do with Israel's God; even unbelievers must reckon with His holiness."},
{q:"What did the priests say must accompany the ark?", options:["A trespass offering, for it must not be sent away empty","A new temple","A golden crown","A peace treaty"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:3",verse:"And they said, If ye send away the ark of the God of Israel, send it not empty; but in any wise return him a trespass offering: then ye shall be healed, and it shall be known to you why his hand is not removed from you.", insight:"Send it not empty; honor is due to God even from His enemies."},
{q:"How many golden emerods and golden mice were required?", options:["Five of each","Seven of each","Twelve of each","Three of each"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:4",verse:"Then said they, What shall be the trespass offering which we shall return to him? They answered, Five golden emerods, and five golden mice, according to the number of the lords of the Philistines: for one plague was on you all, and on your lords.", insight:"Five and five, one for each lord's city; God counts every affliction exactly."},
{q:"Why were the golden images to be made?", options:["To give glory unto the God of Israel","To bribe the Israelites","To honor Dagon","To decorate their temples"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:5",verse:"Wherefore ye shall make images of your emerods, and images of your mice that mar the land; and ye shall give glory unto the God of Israel: peradventure he will lighten his hand from off you, and from off your gods, and from off your land.", insight:"Give glory unto the God of Israel; even pagans learned to honor Him under judgment."},
{q:"What warning did the priests give the Philistine leaders?", options:["Do not harden your hearts, as the Egyptians and Pharaoh did","Do not trust the Israelites","Do not delay the offering","Do not fear the ark"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:6",verse:"Wherefore then do ye harden your hearts, as the Egyptians and Pharaoh hardened their hearts? when he had wrought wonderfully among them, did they not let the people go, and they departed?", insight:"Remember Pharaoh's hardened heart; learning from others' folly is cheaper than your own."},
{q:"What kind of cows were to draw the cart?", options:["Two milch kine on which no yoke had ever come","Two trained oxen","Two heifers from Ekron","Two young bulls"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:7",verse:"Now therefore make a new cart, and take two milch kine, on which there hath come no yoke, and tie the kine to the cart, and bring their calves home from them:", insight:"Never yoked, and their calves shut up at home; the test was set so no one could credit nature for what God would do."},
{q:"Where were the jewels of gold to be placed?", options:["In a coffer by the side of the ark","On the heads of the kine","In Dagon's temple","Under the cart"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:8",verse:"And take the ark of the LORD, and lay it upon the cart; and put the jewels of gold, which ye return him for a trespass offering, in a coffer by the side thereof; and send it away, that it may go.", insight:"A coffer beside the ark; set your best gifts next to what is most holy."},
{q:"How would the Philistines know whether God had smitten them?", options:["If the kine went up by the way of his own coast to Beth-shemesh","If the cart broke apart","If the sky grew dark","If Dagon fell again"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:9",verse:"And see, if it goeth up by the way of his own coast to Beth-shemesh, then he hath done us this great evil: but if not, then we shall know that it is not his hand that smote us; it was a chance that happened to us.", insight:"If it goes to Beth-shemesh, then His hand did this; God does not fear an honest test."},
{q:"What was placed in the coffer with the ark?", options:["The mice of gold and the images of their emerods","Silver vessels","Priestly robes","Bread and wine"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:11",verse:"And they laid the ark of the LORD upon the cart, and the coffer with the mice of gold and the images of their emerods.", insight:"Their shame molded in gold; bring your sins honestly to God and He turns them into testimony."},
{q:"What did the kine do on the road?", options:["Went straight to Beth-shemesh, lowing as they went, turning neither right nor left","Turned back toward Ekron","Wandered into the fields","Stood still and would not move"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:12",verse:"And the kine took the straight way to the way of Beth-shemesh, and went along the highway, lowing as they went, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left; and the lords of the Philistines went after them unto the border of Beth-shemesh.", insight:"Lowing for their calves, they still went straight; God's creatures obey Him better than His people sometimes do."},
{q:"What were the men of Beth-shemesh doing when the ark arrived?", options:["Reaping their wheat harvest in the valley","Holding a war council","Sleeping at noon","Building a wall"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:13",verse:"And they of Beth-shemesh were reaping their wheat harvest in the valley: and they lifted up their eyes, and saw the ark, and rejoiced to see it.", insight:"An ordinary harvest day became holy ground; God breaks into your work with joy."},
{q:"Where did the cart come to rest?", options:["In the field of Joshua, a Beth-shemite, by a great stone","At the city gate","In the temple court","Beside the river"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:14",verse:"And the cart came into the field of Joshua, a Beth-shemite, and stood there, where there was a great stone: and they clave the wood of the cart, and offered the kine a burnt offering unto the LORD.", insight:"By a great stone in Joshua's field; God sets down His mercies in plain sight, where everyone remembers."},
{q:"Who took the ark down from the cart?", options:["The Levites","The Philistine lords","The elders","The reapers"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:15",verse:"And the Levites took down the ark of the LORD, and the coffer that was with it, wherein the jewels of gold were, and put them on the great stone: and the men of Beth-shemesh offered burnt offerings and sacrificed sacrifices the same day unto the LORD.", insight:"The Levites handled the holy things; reverence keeps its proper order."},
{q:"What did the five lords of the Philistines do after seeing the ark delivered?", options:["Returned to Ekron the same day","Followed the ark to Kirjath-jearim","Attacked Beth-shemesh","Worshipped the LORD"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:16",verse:"And when the five lords of the Philistines had seen it, they returned to Ekron the same day.", insight:"They watched and went home; seeing God's work is not the same as bowing to it."},
{q:"Which cities did the five golden emerods represent?", options:["Ashdod, Gaza, Askelon, Gath, and Ekron","Ashdod, Gath, and Hebron","Tyre, Sidon, and Gaza","Ekron and Beth-shemesh"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:17",verse:"And these are the golden emerods which the Philistines returned for a trespass offering unto the LORD; for Ashdod one, for Gaza one, for Askelon one, for Gath one, for Ekron one;", insight:"Five cities, five offerings; judgment had reached every seat of the Philistine lords."},
{q:"What was the great stone in Joshua's field called?", options:["Abel","Ebenezer","Mizpeh","Bethel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:18",verse:"And the golden mice, according to the number of all the cities of the Philistines belonging to the five lords, both of fenced cities, and of country villages, even unto the great stone of Abel, whereon they set down the ark of the LORD: which stone remaineth unto this day in the field of Joshua, the Beth-shemite.", insight:"The stone of Abel remained unto this day; God leaves markers so the story is never lost."},
{q:"Why did the LORD smite the men of Beth-shemesh?", options:["Because they had looked into the ark of the LORD","Because they offered the wrong sacrifice","Because they stole the gold","Because they fled from the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:19",verse:"And he smote the men of Beth-shemesh, because they had looked into the ark of the LORD, even he smote of the people fifty thousand and threescore and ten men: and the people lamented, because the LORD had smitten many of the people with a great slaughter.", insight:"They looked into the ark; holy things are not curiosities, and reverence guards life."},
{q:"What did the men of Beth-shemesh cry out after the slaughter?", options:["Who is able to stand before this holy LORD God?","Let us hide the ark forever","The Philistines are stronger than we","We will serve Dagon"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:20",verse:"And the men of Beth-shemesh said, Who is able to stand before this holy LORD God? and to whom shall he go up from us?", insight:"Who can stand before this holy God? It is a right question; ask it early, not too late."},
{q:"To whom did Beth-shemesh send messengers about the ark?", options:["The inhabitants of Kirjath-jearim","The elders at Shiloh","The Philistine lords","Samuel at Ramah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 6:21",verse:"And they sent messengers to the inhabitants of Kirjath-jearim, saying, The Philistines have brought again the ark of the LORD; come ye down, and fetch it up to you.", insight:"Come and fetch it up; fear passed the ark along until a heart was ready to keep it."}
]},
{n:7, name:"Repentance at Mizpeh", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 7:12",verse:"Then Samuel took a stone, and set it between Mizpeh and Shen, and called the name of it Eben-ezer, saying, Hitherto hath the LORD helped us."}, facts:["Did you know the name Ebenezer means 'stone of help,' and Samuel raised it between Mizpeh and Shen where the LORD had thundered against the Philistines (1 Samuel 7:12)?","Did you know Israel's repentance at Mizpeh was acted out in a symbol: they drew water and poured it out before the LORD, as if their hearts were melting in confession (1 Samuel 7:6)?","Did you know Samuel rode a yearly circuit as judge through Bethel, Gilgal, and Mizpeh, always returning home to Ramah, where he built an altar (1 Samuel 7:16-17)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where was the ark taken after Beth-shemesh?", options:["To the house of Abinadab in the hill at Kirjath-jearim","To Shiloh","To the tabernacle at Gilgal","To Samuel's house at Ramah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:1",verse:"And the men of Kirjath-jearim came, and brought up the ark of the LORD, and brought it into the house of Abinadab in the hill, and sanctified Eleazar his son to keep the ark of the LORD.", insight:"Abinadab's house became its keeper; God rests where He is welcomed."},
{q:"Who was sanctified to keep the ark?", options:["Eleazar, the son of Abinadab","Uzzah","Phinehas","Samuel himself"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:1",verse:"And the men of Kirjath-jearim came, and brought up the ark of the LORD, and brought it into the house of Abinadab in the hill, and sanctified Eleazar his son to keep the ark of the LORD.", insight:"Eleazar was set apart for the task; guarding holy things is itself a calling."},
{q:"How long did the ark abide in Kirjath-jearim?", options:["Twenty years","Seven months","Forty years","Twelve years"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:2",verse:"And it came to pass, while the ark abode in Kirjath-jearim, that the time was long; for it was twenty years: and all the house of Israel lamented after the LORD.", insight:"Twenty years the ark sat waiting; God's people can drift a long time before they lament."},
{q:"What did Samuel call Israel to do first?", options:["Return unto the LORD with all their hearts","Build an altar at Bethel","Choose a king","Offer a thousand sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:3",verse:"And Samuel spake unto all the house of Israel, saying, If ye do return unto the LORD with all your hearts, then put away the strange gods and Ashtaroth from among you, and prepare your hearts unto the LORD, and serve him only: and he will deliver you out of the hand of the Philistines.", insight:"Return with all your hearts; half-hearted turning is no turning at all."},
{q:"What were the people to put away from among them?", options:["The strange gods and Ashtaroth","Their flocks","Their weapons","Their harvest"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:3",verse:"And Samuel spake unto all the house of Israel, saying, If ye do return unto the LORD with all your hearts, then put away the strange gods and Ashtaroth from among you, and prepare your hearts unto the LORD, and serve him only: and he will deliver you out of the hand of the Philistines.", insight:"Put away the idols first; you cannot serve God while clutching your gods."},
{q:"What did the children of Israel do?", options:["Put away Baalim and Ashtaroth, and served the LORD only","Refused Samuel","Fled to Egypt","Made a golden calf"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:4",verse:"Then the children of Israel did put away Baalim and Ashtaroth, and served the LORD only.", insight:"They did it; repentance that acts is repentance that counts."},
{q:"Where did Samuel gather all Israel?", options:["Mizpeh","Bethel","Gilgal","Ramah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:5",verse:"And Samuel said, Gather all Israel to Mizpeh, and I will pray for you unto the LORD.", insight:"Gather to Mizpeh, and I will pray for you; a praying leader gathers a praying people."},
{q:"What did the people do with water at Mizpeh?", options:["Drew water and poured it out before the LORD","Drank it in a feast","Washed the altar with it","Carried it to the ark"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:6",verse:"And they gathered together to Mizpeh, and drew water, and poured it out before the LORD, and fasted on that day, and said there, We have sinned against the LORD. And Samuel judged the children of Israel in Mizpeh.", insight:"Poured out before the LORD; hearts melted like water when confession came."},
{q:"What did the people confess at Mizpeh?", options:["We have sinned against the LORD","The Philistines are too strong","Give us a king","We will not fast"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:6",verse:"And they gathered together to Mizpeh, and drew water, and poured it out before the LORD, and fasted on that day, and said there, We have sinned against the LORD. And Samuel judged the children of Israel in Mizpeh.", insight:"We have sinned; confession by name opens the door to mercy."},
{q:"How did Israel react when the Philistine lords came up against them?", options:["They were afraid","They rejoiced","They attacked at once","They fled to the hills"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:7",verse:"And when the Philistines heard that the children of Israel were gathered together to Mizpeh, the lords of the Philistines went up against Israel. And when the children of Israel heard it, they were afraid of the Philistines.", insight:"Fresh repentance does not banish fear; it turns fear into prayer."},
{q:"What did Israel beg Samuel never to stop doing?", options:["Crying unto the LORD their God for them","Blowing the trumpet","Building the altar","Numbering the people"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:8",verse:"And the children of Israel said to Samuel, Cease not to cry unto the LORD our God for us, that he will save us out of the hand of the Philistines.", insight:"Cease not to cry; keep praying people near you, and never let them stop."},
{q:"What did Samuel offer as a burnt offering?", options:["A sucking lamb, wholly unto the LORD","A bullock","Two doves","A ram"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:9",verse:"And Samuel took a sucking lamb, and offered it for a burnt offering wholly unto the LORD: and Samuel cried unto the LORD for Israel; and the LORD heard him.", insight:"A whole lamb for the whole nation, and the LORD heard him; wholehearted sacrifice brings a whole answer."},
{q:"How did the LORD answer Samuel's cry?", options:["He thundered with a great thunder upon the Philistines","He sent fire from heaven","He parted the sea","He sent an earthquake"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:10",verse:"And as Samuel was offering up the burnt offering, the Philistines drew near to battle against Israel: but the LORD thundered with a great thunder on that day upon the Philistines, and discomfited them; and they were smitten before Israel.", insight:"Great thunder routed the army; when God fights, battles end before they begin."},
{q:"How far did the men of Israel pursue the Philistines?", options:["Until they came under Beth-car","To the sea","To Ekron","To the border of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:11",verse:"And the men of Israel went out of Mizpeh, and pursued the Philistines, and smote them, until they came under Beth-car.", insight:"From Mizpeh to Beth-car; God turns the hunted into the hunters."},
{q:"What did Samuel call the stone he set up?", options:["Eben-ezer","Bethel","Gilgal","Mizpeh"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:12",verse:"Then Samuel took a stone, and set it between Mizpeh and Shen, and called the name of it Eben-ezer, saying, Hitherto hath the LORD helped us.", insight:"Ebenezer, the stone of help; raise markers for answered prayer so you forget less."},
{q:"What does the name Ebenezer declare?", options:["Hitherto hath the LORD helped us","The LORD is our banner","God is my rock","The place of sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:12",verse:"Then Samuel took a stone, and set it between Mizpeh and Shen, and called the name of it Eben-ezer, saying, Hitherto hath the LORD helped us.", insight:"Hitherto the LORD helped us; gratitude looks backward to see forward."},
{q:"What was true of the Philistines for the rest of Samuel's days?", options:["They came no more into the coast of Israel","They ruled over Israel","They intermarried with Israel","They destroyed Mizpeh"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:13",verse:"So the Philistines were subdued, and they came no more into the coast of Israel: and the hand of the LORD was against the Philistines all the days of Samuel.", insight:"The hand of the LORD was against them all Samuel's days; one man's faithfulness can shield a nation."},
{q:"What was restored to Israel?", options:["The cities the Philistines had taken, from Ekron to Gath","The ark to Shiloh","The temple vessels","The lost flocks"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:14",verse:"And the cities which the Philistines had taken from Israel were restored to Israel, from Ekron even unto Gath; and the coasts thereof did Israel deliver out of the hands of the Philistines. And there was peace between Israel and the Amorites.", insight:"Cities restored from Ekron to Gath; repentance recovers what sin surrendered."},
{q:"How long did Samuel judge Israel?", options:["All the days of his life","Forty years","Twenty years","Until Saul was born"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:15",verse:"And Samuel judged Israel all the days of his life.", insight:"All the days of his life; faithful service does not retire."},
{q:"Which places did Samuel visit year by year in his circuit?", options:["Bethel, Gilgal, and Mizpeh","Shiloh, Shechem, and Hebron","Jerusalem, Jericho, and Ai","Dan, Beersheba, and Joppa"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 7:16",verse:"And he went from year to year in circuit to Bethel, and Gilgal, and Mizpeh, and judged Israel in all those places.", insight:"Year by year, the same faithful circuit; steady presence is a ministry."}
]},
{n:8, name:"Give Us a King", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 8:7",verse:"And the LORD said unto Samuel, Hearken unto the voice of the people in all that they say unto thee: for they have not rejected thee, but they have rejected me, that I should not reign over them."}, facts:["Did you know Samuel's sons, Joel and Abiah, judged in Beersheba and stand in Scripture as a warning that godliness is not inherited (1 Samuel 8:2-3)?","Did you know God's answer to Samuel is one of the great comforts for rejected servants: 'they have not rejected thee, but they have rejected me' (1 Samuel 8:7)?","Did you know Israel's stated reason for wanting a king was conformity, 'that we also may be like all the nations,' the very thing God had called them out from (1 Samuel 8:20)?"], questions:[
{q:"When Samuel was old, what did he do?", options:["Made his sons judges over Israel","Anointed Saul","Retired to Egypt","Built the temple"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when Samuel was old, that he made his sons judges over Israel.", insight:"He made his sons judges; even great leaders cannot pass on character by appointment."},
{q:"What were the names of Samuel's sons?", options:["Joel and Abiah","Hophni and Phinehas","Nadab and Abihu","Joab and Abishai"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:2",verse:"Now the name of his firstborn was Joel; and the name of his second, Abiah: they were judges in Beer-sheba.", insight:"Joel and Abiah judged in Beersheba; their names are remembered, but their ways are a warning."},
{q:"How did Samuel's sons conduct themselves?", options:["They turned aside after lucre, took bribes, and perverted judgment","They walked in Samuel's ways","They fled from Israel","They became priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:3",verse:"And his sons walked not in his ways, but turned aside after lucre, and took bribes, and perverted judgment.", insight:"Lucre, bribes, perverted judgment; greed is the shortest road away from God."},
{q:"Who came to Samuel at Ramah?", options:["All the elders of Israel","The Philistine lords","The sons of Belial","The captains of the army"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:4",verse:"Then all the elders of Israel gathered themselves together, and came to Samuel unto Ramah,", insight:"The elders gathered with a real grievance; even good complaints can carry wrong solutions."},
{q:"What did the elders ask Samuel to do?", options:["Make us a king to judge us like all the nations","Give us thy sons as judges","Send us back to Egypt","Build us an altar"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:5",verse:"And said unto him, Behold, thou art old, and thy sons walk not in thy ways: now make us a king to judge us like all the nations.", insight:"Like all the nations; the most dangerous prayer is the one that copies the crowd."},
{q:"How did Samuel answer their request?", options:["The thing displeased him, and he prayed unto the LORD","He rejoiced and anointed a king","He refused to listen","He wept and fled"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:6",verse:"But the thing displeased Samuel, when they said, Give us a king to judge us. And Samuel prayed unto the LORD.", insight:"Displeased, he prayed; take your disappointments to God before you answer men."},
{q:"What did God tell Samuel about the people's rejection?", options:["They have not rejected thee, but they have rejected me, that I should not reign over them","They have rejected thy sons only","They will repent tomorrow","Samuel should resign"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:7",verse:"And the LORD said unto Samuel, Hearken unto the voice of the people in all that they say unto thee: for they have not rejected thee, but they have rejected me, that I should not reign over them.", insight:"Not thee, but Me; when people push God aside, do not take it as your failure."},
{q:"What was Samuel commanded to do before giving them a king?", options:["Protest solemnly unto them, and shew them the manner of the king","Anoint the tallest man","Write their request in a book","Refuse them outright"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:9",verse:"Now therefore hearken unto their voice: howbeit yet protest solemnly unto them, and shew them the manner of the king that shall reign over them.", insight:"Protest solemnly; warn plainly even when people have made up their minds."},
{q:"What would the king do with their sons?", options:["Take them for his chariots, his horsemen, and to run before his chariots","Make them priests","Send them to Egypt","Set them free from labor"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:11",verse:"And he said, This will be the manner of the king that shall reign over you: He will take your sons, and appoint them for himself, for his chariots, and to be his horsemen; and some shall run before his chariots.", insight:"He will take your sons; every throne exacts its price in other people's children."},
{q:"What labor would the king lay upon them?", options:["Plow his ground, reap his harvest, and make his instruments of war","Teach them to read","Send them as ambassadors","Build them houses"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:12",verse:"And he will appoint him captains over thousands, and captains over fifties; and will set them to ear his ground, and to reap his harvest, and to make his instruments of war, and instruments of his chariots.", insight:"Ear his ground and forge his weapons; earthly kingdoms turn free men into servants."},
{q:"What would the king do with their daughters?", options:["Take them to be confectionaries, cooks, and bakers","Make them queens","Send them to the temple","Free them from work"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:13",verse:"And he will take your daughters to be confectionaries, and to be cooks, and to be bakers.", insight:"Confectionaries, cooks, bakers; a king's table is built on other families' daughters."},
{q:"What would the king take of their land?", options:["Their fields, vineyards, and oliveyards, even the best of them","Only the wilderness","Their city houses","Their wells alone"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:14",verse:"And he will take your fields, and your vineyards, and your oliveyards, even the best of them, and give them to his servants.", insight:"Even the best of them; power takes the choicest first."},
{q:"What share of their seed and vineyards would the king take?", options:["The tenth","The half","The firstfruits","Nothing at all"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:15",verse:"And he will take the tenth of your seed, and of your vineyards, and give to his officers, and to his servants.", insight:"The tenth for his officers; weigh what a tenth given to God buys against a tenth taken by a king."},
{q:"What else would the king take for his work?", options:["Their menservants, maidservants, goodliest young men, and asses","Their gold only","Their sons alone","Their flocks alone"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:16",verse:"And he will take your menservants, and your maidservants, and your goodliest young men, and your asses, and put them to his work.", insight:"Your goodliest young men and your asses; the crown consumes the strength of the land."},
{q:"What would the king take of their sheep?", options:["The tenth of their sheep","All of them","None of them","Only the lambs"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:17",verse:"He will take the tenth of your sheep: and ye shall be his servants.", insight:"The tenth of your sheep, and ye shall be his servants; read the fine print of every earthly kingdom."},
{q:"What did Samuel say would happen when they cried out under their king?", options:["The LORD will not hear you in that day","The LORD will send another judge","The king will repent","Samuel will return"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:18",verse:"And ye shall cry out in that day because of your king which ye shall have chosen you; and the LORD will not hear you in that day.", insight:"The LORD will not hear you in that day; choices have echoes that outlast the choosing."},
{q:"How did the people answer Samuel's solemn warning?", options:["Nay; but we will have a king over us","We repent of our request","We will wait for God's time","We choose thy sons instead"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:19",verse:"Nevertheless the people refused to obey the voice of Samuel; and they said, Nay; but we will have a king over us;", insight:"Nay, but we will have a king; a warned heart that will not turn is a sad sight."},
{q:"Why did the people want a king?", options:["That they might be like all the nations, with a king to judge them and fight their battles","To build a temple","To escape the Philistines' taxes","To honor Samuel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:20",verse:"That we also may be like all the nations; and that our king may judge us, and go out before us, and fight our battles.", insight:"Like all the nations; wanting to be like everyone else is the opposite of being set apart."},
{q:"What did Samuel do with all the words of the people?", options:["He rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD","He wrote them in a book","He told the elders","He kept them secret"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:21",verse:"And Samuel heard all the words of the people, and he rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD.", insight:"He rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD; bring people's hard words to God, not just to your pillow."},
{q:"What was the LORD's final word to Samuel?", options:["Hearken unto their voice, and make them a king","Refuse them and rebuke them","Anoint thy eldest son","Send them away"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 8:22",verse:"And the LORD said to Samuel, Hearken unto their voice, and make them a king. And Samuel said unto the men of Israel, Go ye every man unto his city.", insight:"Make them a king; sometimes God grants what we insist on, and teaches us through it."}
]},
{n:9, name:"Saul and the Seer", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 9:16",verse:"To morrow about this time I will send thee a man out of the land of Benjamin, and thou shalt anoint him to be captain over my people Israel, that he may save my people out of the hand of the Philistines: for I have looked upon my people, because their cry is come unto me."}, facts:["Did you know Saul left home to find lost donkeys and walked into a kingdom? The whole chapter turns on one small errand (1 Samuel 9:3).","Did you know the servant's gift for the man of God was only the fourth part of a shekel of silver, yet it carried them to the seer who would anoint a king (1 Samuel 9:8)?","Did you know the chapter pauses to explain that the one now called a prophet was beforetime called a seer in Israel (1 Samuel 9:9)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who was Saul's father?", options:["Kish, a Benjamite, a mighty man of power","Abiel the seer","Zeror the judge","Aphiah the priest"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:1",verse:"Now there was a man of Benjamin, whose name was Kish, the son of Abiel, the son of Zeror, the son of Bechorath, the son of Aphiah, a Benjamite, a mighty man of power.", insight:"Kish, a mighty man of power; God often raises leaders from strong, quiet households."},
{q:"How is Saul described?", options:["A choice young man, and a goodly, higher than any of the people from his shoulders and upward","Short and weak","Old and gray","Lame in both feet"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:2",verse:"And he had a son, whose name was Saul, a choice young man, and a goodly: and there was not among the children of Israel a goodlier person than he: from his shoulders and upward he was higher than any of the people.", insight:"Head and shoulders above them all; God gave Israel the king they wanted to look at."},
{q:"What errand took Saul from home?", options:["To seek his father's lost asses","To buy grain","To visit Samuel","To join the army"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:3",verse:"And the asses of Kish Saul’s father were lost. And Kish said to Saul his son, Take now one of the servants with thee, and arise, go seek the asses.", insight:"Lost asses led to a kingdom; God steers by small errands toward great purposes."},
{q:"Through which lands did Saul pass in his search?", options:["Mount Ephraim, Shalisha, Shalim, and the land of the Benjamites","Judah and Simeon","Gilead and Bashan","The wilderness of Zin"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:4",verse:"And he passed through mount Ephraim, and passed through the land of Shalisha, but they found them not: then they passed through the land of Shalim, and there they were not: and he passed through the land of the Benjamites, but they found them not.", insight:"Four regions and no asses; fruitless searching can still be God's guided tour."},
{q:"Why did Saul want to turn back at the land of Zuph?", options:["Lest his father stop caring for the asses and start worrying about them","Because he was tired","Because the servant quit","Because night was falling"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:5",verse:"And when they were come to the land of Zuph, Saul said to his servant that was with him, Come, and let us return; lest my father leave caring for the asses, and take thought for us.", insight:"Lest my father take thought for us; Saul's first recorded care is for his father's heart."},
{q:"What did the servant propose?", options:["To ask the man of God in the city, whose words surely come to pass","To go home and forget the asses","To buy new asses","To pray at the high place"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:6",verse:"And he said unto him, Behold now, there is in this city a man of God, and he is an honourable man; all that he saith cometh surely to pass: now let us go thither; peradventure he can shew us our way that we should go.", insight:"An honourable man, all that he saith cometh to pass; wise servants point their masters to God."},
{q:"What did the servant have to give the man of God?", options:["The fourth part of a shekel of silver","A gold ring","A lamb","Nothing at all"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:8",verse:"And the servant answered Saul again, and said, Behold, I have here at hand the fourth part of a shekel of silver: that will I give to the man of God, to tell us our way.", insight:"A fourth part of a shekel; small gifts in honest hands open great doors."},
{q:"What was a prophet beforetime called in Israel?", options:["A seer","A scribe","A priest","A judge"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:9",verse:"(Beforetime in Israel, when a man went to enquire of God, thus he spake, Come, and let us go to the seer: for he that is now called a Prophet was beforetime called a Seer.)", insight:"Beforetime called a seer; God has always given His people eyes to see ahead."},
{q:"Whom did Saul and his servant meet going up the hill to the city?", options:["Young maidens going out to draw water","Philistine soldiers","Merchants","Shepherds"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:11",verse:"And as they went up the hill to the city, they found young maidens going out to draw water, and said unto them, Is the seer here?", insight:"Maidens at the well; God plants guides on ordinary roads."},
{q:"What did the maidens say was happening in the city that day?", options:["A sacrifice of the people in the high place","A wedding feast","A battle muster","A market day"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:12",verse:"And they answered them, and said, He is; behold, he is before you: make haste now, for he came to day to the city; for there is a sacrifice of the people to day in the high place:", insight:"A sacrifice that day; God's calendar was already running ahead of Saul's."},
{q:"When had the LORD spoken to Samuel about Saul?", options:["A day before Saul came","A month before","That very morning","A year before"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:15",verse:"Now the LORD had told Samuel in his ear a day before Saul came, saying,", insight:"A day before, in his ear; God prepares the servant before He sends the seeker."},
{q:"What was Samuel told to do with the man from Benjamin?", options:["Anoint him to be captain over Israel, to save them from the Philistines","Make him a priest","Send him home","Give him the ark"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:16",verse:"To morrow about this time I will send thee a man out of the land of Benjamin, and thou shalt anoint him to be captain over my people Israel, that he may save my people out of the hand of the Philistines: for I have looked upon my people, because their cry is come unto me.", insight:"Captain over My people, to save them; God heard Israel's cry even while they chose wrongly."},
{q:"What did the LORD say to Samuel when he saw Saul?", options:["Behold the man whom I spake to thee of! This same shall reign over my people","This is thy servant forever","Send him away","Make him thy son"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:17",verse:"And when Samuel saw Saul, the LORD said unto him, Behold the man whom I spake to thee of! this same shall reign over my people.", insight:"Behold the man; God's appointments are unmistakable to the one who listens."},
{q:"What did Saul ask Samuel in the gate?", options:["Tell me where the seer's house is","Who art thou","Where are my asses","Wilt thou bless me"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:18",verse:"Then Saul drew near to Samuel in the gate, and said, Tell me, I pray thee, where the seer’s house is.", insight:"He asked the seer where the seer lived; we often miss God standing right in front of us."},
{q:"How did Samuel answer Saul?", options:["I am the seer","I am a stranger here","Ask the maidens","I know nothing"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:19",verse:"And Samuel answered Saul, and said, I am the seer: go up before me unto the high place; for ye shall eat with me to day, and to morrow I will let thee go, and will tell thee all that is in thine heart.", insight:"I am the seer; the answer you seek is closer than you think."},
{q:"What did Samuel tell Saul about the lost asses?", options:["They were found three days ago, so set not his mind on them","They were stolen","They died in the wilderness","They were in Zuph"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:20",verse:"And as for thine asses that were lost three days ago, set not thy mind on them; for they are found. And on whom is all the desire of Israel? Is it not on thee, and on all thy father’s house?", insight:"Found three days ago; God had solved the small problem before Saul reached the big calling."},
{q:"How did Saul describe his tribe and his family?", options:["Benjamin, the smallest of the tribes, and his family the least of all","Judah, the royal tribe","Levi, the priestly tribe","Ephraim, the mighty tribe"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:21",verse:"And Saul answered and said, Am not I a Benjamite, of the smallest of the tribes of Israel? and my family the least of all the families of the tribe of Benjamin? wherefore then speakest thou so to me?", insight:"Smallest tribe, least family; God loves to start with the lowly."},
{q:"Where did Samuel seat Saul and his servant at the feast?", options:["In the chiefest place among about thirty bidden guests","At the gate","Outside the city","In the kitchen"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:22",verse:"And Samuel took Saul and his servant, and brought them into the parlour, and made them sit in the chiefest place among them that were bidden, which were about thirty persons.", insight:"The chiefest place; honor from God comes before any crown is worn."},
{q:"What portion did the cook set before Saul?", options:["The shoulder, and that which was upon it","The breast","The whole lamb","Bread only"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:24",verse:"And the cook took up the shoulder, and that which was upon it, and set it before Saul. And Samuel said, Behold that which is left! set it before thee, and eat: for unto this time hath it been kept for thee since I said, I have invited the people. So Saul did eat with Samuel that day.", insight:"The shoulder, kept for him since the people were invited; God reserves portions for the appointed."},
{q:"Why did Samuel bid the servant pass on and ask Saul to stand still?", options:["That he might shew him the word of God","To rest the asses","To wait for the night","To watch the sunset"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 9:27",verse:"And as they were going down to the end of the city, Samuel said to Saul, Bid the servant pass on before us, (and he passed on,) but stand thou still a while, that I may shew thee the word of God.", insight:"Stand thou still a while; God's word comes to those who pause to hear it."}
]},
{n:10, name:"The Anointing of Saul", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 10:24",verse:"And Samuel said to all the people, See ye him whom the LORD hath chosen, that there is none like him among all the people? And all the people shouted, and said, God save the king."}, facts:["Did you know Saul's anointing was private, a vial of oil poured on his head by Samuel, while his choosing was public, by lot before all Israel at Mizpeh (1 Samuel 10:1, 20-21)?","Did you know the proverb 'Is Saul also among the prophets?' was born the day the Spirit of God came upon Saul at the hill, startling everyone who had known him (1 Samuel 10:11-12)?","Did you know Saul's first royal act was restraint: when the children of Belial despised him and brought him no presents, he held his peace (1 Samuel 10:27)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Samuel do to Saul?", options:["Took a vial of oil, poured it upon his head, and kissed him","Set a crown on his head","Gave him a sword","Clothed him in purple"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:1",verse:"Then Samuel took a vial of oil, and poured it upon his head, and kissed him, and said, Is it not because the LORD hath anointed thee to be captain over his inheritance?", insight:"Oil on his head and a kiss; God anoints with tenderness before He burdens with duty."},
{q:"What was the first sign Samuel promised Saul?", options:["Two men by Rachel's sepulchre at Zelzah would tell him the asses were found","Three men with bread","A company of prophets","Thunder from heaven"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:2",verse:"When thou art departed from me to day, then thou shalt find two men by Rachel’s sepulchre in the border of Benjamin at Zelzah; and they will say unto thee, The asses which thou wentest to seek are found: and, lo, thy father hath left the care of the asses, and sorroweth for you, saying, What shall I do for my son?", insight:"Two men at Rachel's tomb; God confirms His call with specific, checkable signs."},
{q:"Whom would Saul meet at the plain of Tabor?", options:["Three men going up to God to Bethel, one with kids, one with loaves, one with wine","An army of Philistines","His father Kish","Samuel's sons"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:3",verse:"Then shalt thou go on forward from thence, and thou shalt come to the plain of Tabor, and there shall meet thee three men going up to God to Bethel, one carrying three kids, and another carrying three loaves of bread, and another carrying a bottle of wine:", insight:"Three men going up to God; provision meets you on the road of obedience."},
{q:"What would the three men give Saul?", options:["Two loaves of bread","Three kids","A bottle of wine","A new garment"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:4",verse:"And they will salute thee, and give thee two loaves of bread; which thou shalt receive of their hands.", insight:"Two loaves from strangers' hands; God feeds His anointed through unexpected hands."},
{q:"What instruments did the company of prophets carry?", options:["A psaltery, a tabret, a pipe, and a harp","Trumpets and cymbals","Drums and lyres","Flutes only"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:5",verse:"After that thou shalt come to the hill of God, where is the garrison of the Philistines: and it shall come to pass, when thou art come thither to the city, that thou shalt meet a company of prophets coming down from the high place with a psaltery, and a tabret, and a pipe, and a harp, before them; and they shall prophesy:", insight:"Music before prophesying; worship tunes the heart to hear God."},
{q:"What would the Spirit of the LORD do to Saul?", options:["Come upon him, and he would prophesy and be turned into another man","Make him invisible","Give him great wealth","Take him to heaven"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:6",verse:"And the Spirit of the LORD will come upon thee, and thou shalt prophesy with them, and shalt be turned into another man.", insight:"Turned into another man; the Spirit does not improve the old man, He makes a new one."},
{q:"Where was Saul to go down and wait seven days for Samuel?", options:["To Gilgal","To Bethel","To Mizpeh","To Gibeah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:8",verse:"And thou shalt go down before me to Gilgal; and, behold, I will come down unto thee, to offer burnt offerings, and to sacrifice sacrifices of peace offerings: seven days shalt thou tarry, till I come to thee, and shew thee what thou shalt do.", insight:"Seven days at Gilgal; waiting on God's servant is part of the anointing."},
{q:"What happened when Saul turned to go from Samuel?", options:["God gave him another heart","He fell to the ground","He forgot everything","He ran home"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:9",verse:"And it was so, that when he had turned his back to go from Samuel, God gave him another heart: and all those signs came to pass that day.", insight:"God gave him another heart; a new calling needs a new heart, and God supplies it."},
{q:"What happened when Saul came to the hill?", options:["The Spirit of God came upon him, and he prophesied among the prophets","He hid in a cave","He fought the Philistines","He built an altar"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:10",verse:"And when they came thither to the hill, behold, a company of prophets met him; and the Spirit of God came upon him, and he prophesied among them.", insight:"He prophesied among them; the Spirit qualifies the unlikely in front of witnesses."},
{q:"What did the people say when they saw Saul prophesying?", options:["Is Saul also among the prophets?","He is possessed","He is a priest now","He has gone mad"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:11",verse:"And it came to pass, when all that knew him beforetime saw that, behold, he prophesied among the prophets, then the people said one to another, What is this that is come unto the son of Kish? Is Saul also among the prophets?", insight:"Is Saul also among the prophets? When God changes a man, even his neighbors notice."},
{q:"How did one bystander explain the wonder?", options:["But who is their father?","He is Kish's son","Ask Samuel","He learned it in school"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:12",verse:"And one of the same place answered and said, But who is their father? Therefore it became a proverb, Is Saul also among the prophets?", insight:"Who is their father? God needs no pedigree to pour out His Spirit."},
{q:"What did Saul tell his uncle about his visit with Samuel?", options:["That the asses were found, but he said nothing of the kingdom","Everything Samuel had said","Nothing at all","That he had been anointed king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:16",verse:"And Saul said unto his uncle, He told us plainly that the asses were found. But of the matter of the kingdom, whereof Samuel spake, he told him not.", insight:"He told of the asses, not the kingdom; some callings are kept quiet until God's hour."},
{q:"Where did Samuel call the people together unto the LORD?", options:["Mizpeh","Gilgal","Bethel","Ramah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:17",verse:"And Samuel called the people together unto the LORD to Mizpeh;", insight:"To Mizpeh, unto the LORD; public callings are confirmed before God and the people."},
{q:"What charge did Samuel lay upon Israel?", options:["Ye have this day rejected your God, who saved you out of all your adversities","Ye have honored your God","Ye have kept the covenant","Ye have loved Samuel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:19",verse:"And ye have this day rejected your God, who himself saved you out of all your adversities and your tribulations; and ye have said unto him, Nay, but set a king over us. Now therefore present yourselves before the LORD by your tribes, and by your thousands.", insight:"Ye have rejected your God; honesty about the past must come before blessing in the future."},
{q:"Which tribe was taken when Samuel brought them near by tribes?", options:["Benjamin","Judah","Ephraim","Levi"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:20",verse:"And when Samuel had caused all the tribes of Israel to come near, the tribe of Benjamin was taken.", insight:"Benjamin was taken; God's lot found the smallest tribe, just as Samuel had said."},
{q:"Which family was taken, and what happened when they sought Saul?", options:["The family of Matri was taken, and Saul could not be found","The family of Kish, and Saul fled","The family of Abiel, and Saul hid in a cave","The family of Zeror, and Saul was missing"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:21",verse:"When he had caused the tribe of Benjamin to come near by their families, the family of Matri was taken, and Saul the son of Kish was taken: and when they sought him, he could not be found.", insight:"Taken by lot, yet nowhere found; the chosen king was hiding from his own choosing."},
{q:"Where had Saul hidden himself?", options:["Among the stuff","In a well","Behind the altar","In his father's house"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:22",verse:"Therefore they enquired of the LORD further, if the man should yet come thither. And the LORD answered, Behold, he hath hid himself among the stuff.", insight:"Among the stuff; greatness that hides must be fetched by God."},
{q:"What did the people see when Saul stood among them?", options:["He was higher than any of the people from his shoulders and upward","He wore a crown","He carried a sword","He wept"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:23",verse:"And they ran and fetched him thence: and when he stood among the people, he was higher than any of the people from his shoulders and upward.", insight:"Head and shoulders above them all; the outside matched the office, for a season."},
{q:"What did all the people shout when Samuel presented Saul?", options:["God save the king","Long live Samuel","Blessed be Benjamin","Hosanna"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:24",verse:"And Samuel said to all the people, See ye him whom the LORD hath chosen, that there is none like him among all the people? And all the people shouted, and said, God save the king.", insight:"God save the king; the nation received the king it asked for, with God's hand still on him."},
{q:"How did Saul answer the children of Belial who despised him?", options:["He held his peace","He had them killed","He rebuked them","He fled to Gibeah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 10:27",verse:"But the children of Belial said, How shall this man save us? And they despised him, and brought him no presents. But he held his peace.", insight:"He held his peace; the anointed need not answer every critic."}
]}
]);
